commit a0edc5709184f7ce9f4402762e21d5bf4ccfa461
Author: Eshan I. <79593316+eshankiyer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Tue Aug 4 12:28:19 2026 -0400

    fix(worldgen): short-circuit coral mushroom RNG draw on shape check
    
    pumpkin-world/src/generation/feature/features/coral/coral_mushroom.rs
    called random.next_f32() unconditionally on every (m, n, o) grid cell,
    even when the four shape conditions already failed.
    
    Vanilla's CoralMushroomFeature.placeFeature (CoralMushroomFeature.java
    ~L29-34) chains all checks with Java's short-circuiting &&, so
    random.nextFloat() is only drawn once the shape conditions hold. The
    previous Rust port always drew from the RNG regardless, desyncing the
    seeded random stream from vanilla for every subsequent feature/
    decorator sharing it in the chunk.
    
    Fixed by moving the random draw into the same short-circuited
    condition chain, evaluated left-to-right exactly like the Java
    original, so it is skipped whenever an earlier shape condition is
    false. RNG call-count-based testing was not added: RandomGenerator has
    no instrumentable/mock variant in this codebase to assert draw counts
    without a broader test harness change.

