commit c34720644be78ce72a443b2aa5756b831d02b953
Author: Eshan I. <79593316+eshankiyer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Tue Aug 4 12:27:40 2026 -0400

    fix(worldgen): correct coral mushroom position doubling bug
    
    pumpkin-world/src/generation/feature/features/coral/coral_mushroom.rs
    computed the per-cell candidate position by offsetting the already-
    mutated `pos` by (pos.x + m, pos.y + n, pos.z + o), which is a delta
    applied to itself: the result was origin*2 + (m, n, o) instead of
    origin + (m, n, o).
    
    Vanilla's CoralMushroomFeature.placeFeature (CoralMushroomFeature.java
    ~L27) computes the candidate as an absolute offset from the untouched
    origin each iteration: mutPos.set(x + origin.getX(), y + origin.getY(),
    z + origin.getZ()). Fixed by computing `candidate` directly from the
    original `pos` parameter each iteration, without feeding a mutated
    position back into itself.
    
    Adds a unit test asserting the corrected offset arithmetic against a
    sample origin.

